anges, computed from the metering data per the agreed reporting data\n51\t  contract (project attribution and aggregation rules).\n52\t- Current-month admin view showing each project's consumption against its\n53\t  Kueue quota, using the validated per-project quota reference and GPU-hour\n54\t  attribution semantics.\n55\t- CSV export of reports.\n56\t- Stable API exposing report data for retrieval by finance tooling.\n57\t- Administrator-only visibility of the chargeback reporting views, consistent\n58\t  with platform RBAC.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- Administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over\n63\t  selectable time ranges.\n64\t- The admin view shows current-month consumption against each project's Kueue\n65\t  quota.\n66\t- Reports can be exported as CSV.\n67\t- Report data is retrievable via a stable API usable by finance tooling.\n68\t- The chargeback reporting views are visible only to administrators, per\n69\t  platform RBAC.\n70\t- Report values are computed from the metering data per the agreed reporting\n71\t  data contract — no collection logic is re-implemented in the Dashboard.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-1 (P0): per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time\n76\t  ranges.\n77\t- HLR-2 (P1, bundled with HLR-1): CSV export and stable API are retrieval\n78\t  modes of the same report surface and data.\n79\t- HLR-3 (P1, view side): current-month consumption against each project's\n80\t  Kueue quota in the Dashboard admin view.\n81\t\n82\t## Risks / Notes\n83\t\n84\t- External timing risk: this work is gated on the finalized metering data\n85\t  schema from the in-flight GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990); if\n86\t  the finalized schema does not support the reporting needs, the\n87\t  implementation is rewritten against the actual schema shape (or extensions\n88\t  are requested to the metering strategy) before proceeding.\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-t