text file covers Documentation. No arithmetic checked\n(computed by the pipeline). All four ai-signals rationale files present with\nrationales matching frontmatter values.\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\nEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the HLRs. Rule-mandated ACs present\nwhere applicable: E004 (docs-authoring) has the technical-review AC (Rule 26);\nno replacement or konflux-chain epics exist, so Rules 24/25 do not apply. No\nsoft ACs: E001's \"confirmed with the metering data owners\" AC conditions on\nthe epic's own deliverable (the negotiated contract), not an\nexternally-granted availability. No draft-ID references in epic bodies (E001-\nE004 appear only in frontmatter fields, where they are the canonical epic\nidentifiers).\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\nAll strategy scope is accounted for: reporting view, current-month-vs-quota\nview, CSV export, stable API, admin-only visibility, and documentation all\nappear in epic scope/ACs; out-of-scope items (metering collection,\ncurrency/cost modelling) are correctly excluded. The strategy's open question\n(schema finalization timing) is carried forward as E001's gate and E003's\nrisk note, not silently dropped; the data-access-path gap and stable-API\ncommitment are recorded in Health Warnings. Cross-epic consistency holds:\nE002's quota mapping and attribution semantics are consumed by E003 and\ndocumented by E004. No conditional branches are declared, and none are needed\n(no bounded outcome sets in the strategy). HLR-4's documentation requirement\nis met by the docs-authoring epic E004.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":29315,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ec23ba8869c0563","agent_id":"ad290b1da8947b66e","session_id":"ae63a1c3-308e-4096-a1af-f3bfa0f3fcf1","uuid":"76b67cc2-967a-4cf3-8527-cf589be57dc2","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:08:26.038Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","tas