{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-abdd2e079f1e1921","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n3\ttitle: Per-project Kueue quota reference and GPU-hour attribution semantics\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Per-project Kueue quota reference and GPU-hour attribution semantics\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tDelivers the Distributed Workloads side of the chargeback reporting\n34\tcapability: a validated per-project Kueue quota reference (per-project quota\n35\ttotals derived from the platform's ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model) and\n36\tthe agreed GPU-hour attribution semantics — what counts as a GPU-hour relative\n37\tto Kueue quota admission and usage — that the administrator reporting view and\n38\tthe report documentation build on. The component itself keeps working with no\n39\tcollection changes; the metering pipeline is out of scope (RHAISTRAT-9990).\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Define and validate the mapping from the Kueue quota model\n44\t  (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue) to per-project quota totals, covering every\n45\t  project that holds quota.\n46\t- Define the GPU-hour attribution semantics for chargeback reporting: how\n47\t  consumed GPU-hours are attributed to projects relative to quota admission\n48\t  and usage, i.e. what counts as a GPU-hour for reporting purposes.\n49\t- Validate both the quota mapping and the attribution semantics against\n50\t  representative quota configurations.\n51\t- Deliver the validated quota reference and semantics as a contract that the\n52\t  Dashboard reporting view and the documentation can build against.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Per-project quota totals can be derived for every project holding a\n57\t  LocalQueue, with the derivation rules documented.\n58\t- The GPU-hour attribution semantics are documented and validated against\n59\t  representative quota configurations.\n60\t- The validated quota reference and attribution semantics are delivered in a\n61\t  form the Dashboard reporting view can build against.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- HLR-3 (P1, quota side): provides the per-project Kueue quota reference that\n66\t  current-month consumption is compared against.\n67\t- Grounds the report semantics documented under HLR-4 (what counts as a\n68\t  GPU-hour).\n69\t\n70\t## Notes\n71\t\n72\t- This is a validation deliverable owned by the Distributed Workloads team as\n73\t  the owner of the Kueue quota model; it involves no metering collection work\n74\t  (owned by RHAISTRAT-9990) and no currency/cost-rate modelling (out of scope).\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a9b8e6182f098a6","agent_id":"a3e018191f58e0c6d","session_id":"ae63a1c3-308e-4096-a1af-f3bfa0f3fcf1","uuid":"1c690ccb-4e93-45a8-bd10-9a8c3a53dae5","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:09:36.936Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-abdd2e079f1e1921","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
