{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f02c14a89f0152b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate GPU usage metering data schema for chargeback reporting\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Validate GPU usage metering data schema for chargeback reporting\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThe GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990) is in flight and owns the\n30\tper-project GPU-hour usage data schema, which is not final until that strategy\n31\tlands. This investigation resolves the strategy's open question — the external\n32\ttiming and shape of that schema — by tracking it as it stabilizes and\n33\tvalidating that it can support administrator chargeback reporting. It produces\n34\tthe reporting-side data contract that the reporting implementation builds\n35\tagainst: which fields are consumed, the per-project aggregation rules, and how\n36\treporting accesses the metering data.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Map the finalized (or latest draft) metering data schema field-by-field\n41\t  against the reporting needs: per-project GPU-hour totals, selectable time\n42\t  ranges, and current-month windows.\n43\t- Identify gaps where the schema cannot support reporting (project\n44\t  attribution, time granularity, GPU-hour definition) and raise them to the\n45\t  metering strategy owners, with each gap's disposition recorded.\n46\t- Define the reporting-side data contract: consumed fields, per-project\n47\t  aggregation rules, and the access path by which reporting reads the metering\n48\t  data.\n49\t- Record the agreed contract as the deliverable that downstream reporting work\n50\t  builds against, including a go/no-go conclusion.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A written schema-to-reporting mapping exists covering every field the\n55\t  reporting needs (project identity, GPU-hours, timestamps), with each need\n56\t  marked supported or gap.\n57\t- Every gap has a recorded disposition: accepted limitation, or extension\n58\t  request formally raised to the metering strategy owners.\n59\t- The reporting data contract (consumed fields, aggregation rules, access\n60\t  path) is documented and confirmed with the metering data owners.\n61\t- A go/no-go conclusion is recorded: the finalized schema either supports\n62\t  per-project GPU-hour reporting over selectable time ranges, or the required\n63\t  extensions have been formally requested.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- Enables HLR-1, HLR-2, and HLR-3 by resolving the strategy's open question on\n68\t  metering data schema finalization; this investigation does not itself\n69\t  implement any HLR.\n70\t\n71\t## Risks / Notes\n72\t\n73\t- External timing risk: the schema finalizes only when RHAISTRAT-9990 lands.\n74\t  The investigation can start against drafts but cannot conclude before\n75\t  finalization; the timing is outside this strategy's control.\n76\t- The Dashboard owns no data plane (Kubernetes API only per architecture\n77\t  context), so the contract must also settle how reporting accesses\n78\t  time-series metering data, not just its schema.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a9b8e6182f098a6","agent_id":"a3e018191f58e0c6d","session_id":"ae63a1c3-308e-4096-a1af-f3bfa0f3fcf1","uuid":"c5d8cca7-17d3-4879-a914-9e2bd112080d","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:10:38.457Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f02c14a89f0152b",