{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b70e0699bd1a0bb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n3\ttitle: Per-project Kueue quota reference and GPU-hour attribution semantics\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Per-project Kueue quota reference and GPU-hour attribution semantics\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tDelivers the Distributed Workloads side of the chargeback reporting\n34\tcapability: a validated per-project Kueue quota reference (per-project quota\n35\ttotals derived from the platform's ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model) and\n36\tthe agreed GPU-hour attribution semantics — what counts as a GPU-hour relative\n37\tto Kueue quota admission and usage. The quota reference is delivered as a\n38\tmachine-readable runtime artifact — per-project quota totals exported as\n39\tversioned Prometheus metrics from the Distributed Workloads side, extending\n40\tthe existing Kueue-metrics-to-Prometheus pattern — and the attribution\n41\tsemantics as a versioned written definition in the owning repository; the\n42\tadministrator reporting view and the report documentation build on both. The\n43\tcomponent itself keeps working with no\n44\tcollection changes; the metering pipeline is out of scope (RHAISTRAT-9990).\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Define and validate the mapping from the Kueue quota model\n49\t  (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue) to per-project quota totals, covering every\n50\t  project that holds quota.\n51\t- Define the GPU-hour attribution semantics for chargeback reporting: how\n52\t  consumed GPU-hours are attributed to projects relative to quota admission\n53\t  and usage, i.e. what counts as a GPU-hour for reporting purposes.\n54\t- Validate both the quota mapping and the attribution semantics against\n55\t  representative quota configurations.\n56\t- Deliver the validated quota reference as a machine-readable runtime\n57\t  artifact: per-project quota totals exposed as versioned Prometheus metrics\n58\t  (documented metric names and labels) from the Distributed Workloads side,\n59\t  extending the existing Kueue-metrics-to-Prometheus pattern, so the Dashboard\n60\t  reporting view consumes them programmatically rather than re-deriving quota\n61\t  from CRs.\n62\t- Deliver the attribution semantics as a versioned written definition in the\n63\t  owning repository that the report documentation incorporates.\n64\t\n65\t## Acceptance Criteria\n66\t\n67\t- Per-project quota totals can be derived for every project holding a\n68\t  LocalQueue, with the derivation rules documented.\n69\t- The GPU-hour attribution semantics are documented and validated against\n70\t  representative quota configurations.\n71\t- Per-project quota totals are exposed as versioned Prometheus metrics with\n72\t  documented metric names and labels, queryable for every project holding a\n73\t  LocalQueue — a runtime artifact the Dashboard reporting view consumes\n74\t  programmatically, not a prose-only specification.\n75\t- The GPU-hour attribution semantics are recorded as a versioned written\n76\t  definition in the owning repository.\n77\t\n78\t## HLR Traceability\n79\t\n80\t- HLR-3 (P1, quota side): provides the per-project Kueue quota reference that\n81\t  current-month consumption is compared against.\n82\t- Grounds the report semantics documented under HLR-4 (what counts as a\n83\t  GPU-hour).\n84\t\n85\t## Notes\n86\t\n87\t- This is a validation deliverable owned by the Distributed Workloads team as\n88\t  the owner of the Kueue quota model; it involves no metering collection work\n89\t  (owned by RHAISTRAT-9990) and no currency/cost-rate modelling (out of scope).\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b141696f684ec1a","agent_id":"ae4f1820ab5e141a7","session_id":"ae63a1c3-308e-4096-a1af-f3bfa0f3fcf1","uuid":"b8e8f342-e51b-4e3b-b1d1-44207639157c","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:11:50.612Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b70e0699bd1a0bb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
